## 4. Exclusion List

These must NOT appear in the draft:

- Generic "AI is transforming every industry" framing without specificity — John explicitly pushes back on this
- Technical explanations of how LLMs work — the target audience (CTO, VP) does not need this
- Job replacement as the primary AI narrative — John reframes AI as capability enhancement, not headcount reduction, and any return to this framing undermines his argument
- Comparisons of AI vendors by capability or benchmark — not John's territory and not what this article is about
- "10 steps to implement AI" listicle structure — contradicts the article's premise that there is no universal playbook
- Adjacent topics John didn't emphasize: AI regulation/legislation, AI ethics, AI hallucination as a standalone topic (mentioned only in passing)
- Speculative predictions about AGI or long-horizon AI futures — John explicitly grounds this in current, practical business decisions
- The food science company story as a primary example — John did not own this story and provided no specifics

